    "result_text": "The full suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented rejection of a create-owner request whose normalized telephone is already used by another owner, responding **409 Conflict**. Following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions:\n\n**New pipeline step** \u2014 added `rejectDuplicate` to `owners.POST.yml`, placed after `normalize` (so the request telephone is already reduced to digits) and before `build`/`save`, under `govern: [ transaction ]` like the surrounding steps.\n\n**New files:**\n- `RejectDuplicateTelephone.java` \u2014 reads the normalized request via `@Val OwnerFieldsDto`, scans existing owners from `OwnerRepository.findAll()`, normalizing each stored telephone the same way (strip non-digits) so numbers in any format match, and throws when a collision is found.\n- `DuplicateTelephoneException.java` \u2014 a checked exception (`extends Exception`), matching the pattern of the sibling `InvalidTelephoneException`.\n- `DuplicateTelephoneExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 the escalation handler responding `409 CONFLICT`.\n- The escalation YAML wiring the exception to its handler under `officefloor/escalation/`.\n\nBoth new acceptance tests (`coreRejectsDuplicateTelephone`, `functionalityAllowsDistinctTelephone`) and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
